{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1504075-sidereal-office-charms","id":1504075,"title":"Sidereal Office Charms","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-02-28T15:12:58-08:00","id":1504075,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon1.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Sidereal Office Charms","content":"While reading through Ex3 Sidereal charms, I noticed a lack of charms that involved the Sidereal's most defining aspect: Being an office wagie. If you're under the employ of heaven, why not have some charms that make use of that fact?<br /> <br /> <b>Sidebar: Nnnnnooooo! Sidereals shouldn't have new charms</b><br /> <br /> Click on my homebrew signature. Do I look like a man who gives a shit about such things?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Harmonious Review of Performance</b></span><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 5m 1WP; <b>Mins</b>: Bureaucracy 4, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type</b>: Simple<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: None<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms</b>: Icy Hand<br /> <br /> <i>By contacting the archives of heaven, the Sidereal pulls up a spirits\u2019 personal record.</i><br /> <br /> The Sidereal rolls (Perception + Bureaucracy) against the Guile of any spirit. Success grants the Sidereal access to a Meticulous Performance Review (detailed below) sometime in the following day that contains the Spirit\u2019s name, their purview, the spirit\u2019s superior, and where their currently assigned area is.<br /> <br /> For every two threshold successes on the Sidereal\u2019s roll, the Sidereal may ask one of the following additional questions:<ul><li>Declare the report was retroactively arranged for delivery. The Sidereal may gather the report somewhere nearby in a location that\u2019s no more than an inconvenient task to reach</li> <li>What are the last noteworthy activities performed by the spirit?</li> <li>What is the spirit\u2019s current income?</li> <li>What are the last major business expenditures performed by the spirit? (Any currency works, not just ambrosia from heaven)</li> <li>How does the spirit conduct their business? (Information on how they perform their job)</li> <li>Has there been any major or noteworthy obstacles that hampered a spirits\u2019 job within the last year?</li> <li>Any major blessings or curses bestowed by the deity within the last year, including when, where, and who.</li> <li>Is the spirit a part of any conventions or other organizations/clubs that have political and/or military power.</li> <li>Areas the spirit could improve upon on their job.</li> </ul><br /> By default this report is for all information in the last year, but by spending another two successes in a category, the Sidereal can gather information reaching back to a decade. Another two successes grants them information heading back over a century. All information contained within such reports are information the spirit voluntarily submitted to heaven and was approved by who they report to. Such information could be inaccurate, but such reports are invaluable pieces of evidence for tracking down possible corruption. If the Storyteller has no information for the questions, then the Sidereal\u2019s player may declare information as a fact.<br /> <br /> This charm only works on spirits, but if the Sidereal is leading an organization or has some method to exert significant influence over it (by being the trusted advisor to a Guild Factor for example) then the Sidereal many use this charm for any mortal organization, provided at least one year has passed for the first reports to come in. It is no secret that Bronze Faction Sidereals have implemented such a thing within the Realm\u2019s bureaucracy for quite some time now.<br /> <br /> At Essence 3+, any Backing a Sidereal has in a Bureau which belongs to a god they\u2019re requesting a report from adds non-charm dice equal to the backing ranking.<br /> <br /> <b>I like to see more of the question-related charms from Essence, so I felt this was a natural fit. If you're an agent with nigh unrestricted power, then calling HR and pulling up their personal record is the quickest way of getting such information. The bit about MPR's below is somewhat wordy but it's meant to tell Storyteller's that yes, <i>every</i> spirit who works for heaven in some capacity does these. I'm not sure about the placement of this charm though. Originally I was looking at Occult or Investigation, but I decided on Bureaucracy for simplicity.</b><br /> <br /> <i><u>Sidebar: Meticulous Performance Review</u></i><br /> <br /> A Meticulous Performance Review (MPR) is a report that every spirit that works in or for Heaven is required to complete. Originally divised by Sol as a method of recording even the slightest improvements to his limitless excellence, he quickly made a standard for all spirits in heaven shortly after the defeat of the Primordials (I\u2019m not calling them the Ancients). In the first three months of Air after calibration, spirits are expected to draft a document outlying the goals they wish to achieve for their work this year. During Respledent or Descending Earths spirits are expected to meet with their superiors to review whenever or not a spirit has met the stated goals along with any other professional developments they have made during the year. Minor gods may have MPR\u2019s of only a few pages, while MPR\u2019s by high ranking gods such as Ryzala can easily be over 100 pages. All MPR\u2019s are expected to be reviewed by the spirits superior then submitted before the beginning of Calibration, with <i>very</i> few exceptions. Spirits who have direct reports in Creation often send representatives to gather such reports.<br /> <br /> MPR\u2019s are the one piece of work that heaven tracks very closely. If a MPR is not submitted, the Bureau of Heaven will remind the god to submit them. From the lowiliest city god to even the Incarnae. Failure to do so will result in the gods wage being garnished. If a few months go by, the spirits superior will be notified (with the spirits\u2019 superior also being punished if no action is taken). If another year goes by without such a report, then such gods are summoned for a formal audit of what they did the previous year. When the Unconquered Sun turned his back on Creation and spiralled into a deep depression, he too was eventually summoned for an audit, which even the long lived spirits in heaven call the most awkward performance audit they ever had to perform. Bizarrely, this bolstered many spirits faith in the Unconquered Sun as it showed he too was willing to be held accountable.<br /> <br /> MPR\u2019s are intended to contain truthful information, but in reality that\u2019s hardly the case. The smallest of accomplishes are mentioned as epic feats, the decision to get silver instead of gold office furnishings are recorded as unprecedented cost cutting business expenses, while planning an office tea party counts as a new frontier of leadership. MPR\u2019s are only expected to relate to a spirit\u2019s professional development at their job, personal matters need not be mentioned (unless they involve the spirit\u2019s job). While stretching the truth isn\u2019t an offense, lying on these reports is. Any false information on these reports could allow the god to be processed with any crimes or fines that is appropriate for filing false paperwork.<br /> <br /> As agents of Heaven, Sidereals are expected to do such reports as well. Because of the nature of arcane fate, Such reports are assumed to be done off camera, unless a character is deliberately avoiding them for some reason. Sidereals (and other spirits) who are on long term assignments do not need to submit such reports, but are expected to file them when they have reasonable time to do so. Sidereals cannot request the MPR\u2019s of other Sidereals, but may request those of their previous incarnation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Seredipitous Happenstance Clue</span></b><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 5m 1WP; <b>Mins</b>: Investigation 4, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type</b>: Simple<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: None<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms</b>: Marvelous Inclusion of Details<br /> <br /> <i>When finds themselves unable to proceed, fate ensures they will have a way forward.</i><br /> <br /> The Sidereal asks a question related to their current circumstances then rolls (Perception + Investigation) against a difficulty assigned by the Storyteller. If successful the Sidereal happens to run across an event that provides the Sidereal the information they need, but other rolls may be required to extract the required information.<br /> <br /> A guideline of the difficulties involved with this charm is as follows:<ul><li>Difficulty 3: Information that is hidden but only hidden by mundane efforts or information that has only mild importance or consequences for knowing. Requesting to know the hidden escape route of a King, wanting to know the password to a secret club in Firewander that contains disgruntled workers,</li> <li>Difficulty 5:Information that is hidden by potent supernatural creatures who wish to have their information remain hidden and whose knowledge carries danger even to an Exalt. Knowing the rout through an illusionary maze of mirrors to an underground Raksha bazaar, knowing the password to a yozi cult hostile towards the uninitiated.</li> <li>Difficulty 7: Information that is hidden by very powerful entities who have a vested interest in it remaining hidden and has dramatic consequences for knowing. Knowing the safe path through an ancient First Age manse that contains numerous Deathtraps, knowing the time and location for a secret meeting by a high ranking god, the activation codes for a Thousand Forged Dragon.</li> </ul>If a character fails this charm, they are not outright denied the information. Rather the Storyteller provides the Sidereal a leading clue or direction to where such information could be.<br /> <br /> This charm is meant to aid investigations, not simply hand the keys to them. Instead of revealing the whole mystery, the Storyteller may instead allow players a vital clue or a method of continuing an Investigation after a player has run out of leads.<br /> <br /> This charm may be used once per case the Sidereal is involved with or per day. The Maiden of Secrets is not against providing their chosen assistance, but she\u2019d rather her chosen uncover hidden knowledge with their own ingenuity and cunning.<br /> <br /> <i>Example: Seven Veiled Shadows needs to gain access to a Lord\u2019s castle in order to complete his mission, but even wearing a Resplendent Destiny the guards firmly insist no one is allowed inside without a password. Seven Veiled Shadows activates Seredipitous Happenstance Clue and gains four successes on the roll. The Storyteller narrates that Seven Veiled Shadows overhears a conversation between two nearby guards about a password, and asks for an Awareness to listen in closer or a stealth roll to get closer to listen. Seven Veiled Shadows successfully makes the Awareness roll, allowing him to listen in to the conversation. Guard A forgot the password but doesn\u2019t want to ask his superior as he\u2019d be yelled at again, Guard B sighs and tells him the password to the Lord\u2019s personal office along with a warning that this is the last time he\u2019ll be doing this.<br /> <br /> Serenade of Venusday has infiltrated a Silver Pact\u2019s Lunar\u2019s hidden lair, looking for a map that is rumoured to contain a hidden manse with a functioning Factory-Cathedral from the First Age. Serenade activates Seredipitous Happenstance Clue and rolls 7 successes. Later during her infiltration, the Storyteller says Serenade runs across a study and she notices a Lunar sage reading an encrypted letter from his superiors. Serenade knows the letter contains the information she wants, but she\u2019ll either need to steal the letter and break the encryption or convince the Lunar Sage to give her the information.</i><br /> <br /> <b>This charm is based off video game logic where you character ALWAYS just happens to find the information you're searching for nearby. Efficient Secretary Technique (EFS) is a damn powerful charm, so rather than compete against it I decided it's best to make charms that complement EFS. Can't find hidden thing? Make it so hidden thing is nearby.</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Flawless Briefing Preparation</span></b><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 5m 1WP; <b>Mins</b>: Lore 3, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type</b>: Simple<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: Divination<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms</b>: Systematic Understanding of Everything<br /> <br /> <i>With careful foresight, a Sidereal makes arrangements to learn what he needs to know during the most crucial part of their assignment.</i><br /> <br /> The Sidereal declares a fact or piece of information they wish to know, rolling (Intelligence+Lore) against a difficulty the player wishes to know about. Success retroactively generates a briefing document for the Sidereal on a subject of their choosing. The Sidereal will have commissioned this briefing note the last time he was in or communicated with someone in heaven retroactively sometime in the past. Agents of heaven will have hidden this briefing note according to the Sidereal\u2019s instructions, which upon activating this charm will be somewhere nearby the Sidereal\u2019s current location. This document will require the Sidereal to perform a task that\u2019s no more than an inconvenient task to retrieve.<br /> <br /> This briefing note will contain clear and succinct information. The Sidereal counts as having access to any of their Allies, Contacts, Mentor, or any other relevant mertis that are capable of providing informations, as the clerk who writes the briefing note will consult all appropriate characters and resources to gather the information contained within the document. Treat any information gathered as if it were well researched in a large, well supplied library.<br /> <br /> For every two threshold successes on the roll, the Sidereal may ask one of the following questions. If a question does not have an answer, the Sidereal\u2019s player may introduce one as if it were a fact.<ul><li>History and background information on a person/place/thing Heaven is aware of</li> <li>What is the destiny of a person/place/thing?</li> <li>Has Heaven had any interactions with the person/place/thing in any official capacity?</li> <li>Who were the major/notable players in a historical event, organization, or current location?</li> <li>Has there been any notable interferences in Fate the Sidereal was not informed of ahead of time?</li> <li>Recommendations on how to proceed with a certain course of action for a desired effect (The Sidereal may have an Ally/Mentor in heaven make such recommendations)</li> </ul>Once the Sidereal has had a chance to read the document, it bursts into flames. The Sidereal can make a special request to have the document not incinerate upon reading it, but players be warned: These documents are exclusively for those within the bureau of destiny. If any character outside the bureau of destiny reads these documents then it is grounds for immediate audit, with punishment depending on the severity. A Sidereal showing their Solar circlemate a briefing note on what Heaven thinks of them might be a small punishment, but showing detailed information of a Kingdom\u2019s planned downfall to a King might be grounds for a far more severe punishment. This punishment also applies to any spirit within Heaven, as few spirits in heaven are brazen enough to intercept and read top secret documents from a Bureau. All reports a Sidereal request have a permanent copy stored within the Bureau of Destiny\u2019s archives.<br /> <br /> If the Sidereal fails this roll, then they will either find a note indicating the report is not yet completed or will be heavily redacted and provide basic information. This charm can only be used once per story, but it may be refreshed upon learning a significant piece of information without Heaven\u2019s help.<br /> <br /> <u><i>Sidebar: Can I get other Bureau\u2019s to write briefing notes for me?</i></u><br /> <br /> Yes, you can. If a Sidereal has either Backing 3 within a Bureau or has a major god within that Bureau as an Ally/Mentor, other Bureau\u2019s can write briefing notes for the Sidereal. This can allow for additional information or information provided from a new lens other than the Bureau of Destiny. This could also allow for less redactions within certain areas.<br /> <br /> <b>I can see some overlap with Efficient Secretary Technique (EST), but this is for a different purpose. Imagine having access to a well-stocked library and relevant Allies/Mentors for information at any time? EST is certainly nice, but this provides a one-time pass for very detailed information.<br /> <br /> Also spies needing to go out of their way to retrieve documents hidden by their headquarters is a cool thing to do.\u200b</b><br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-28T15:45:24-08:00","id":1504079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1504075-sidereal-office-charms#post1504075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While reading through Ex3 Sidereal charms, I noticed a lack of charms that involved the Sidereal's most defining aspect: Being an office wagie.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>It's 2008... my time machine worked!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}